Chapter: CapDeviceDeclared

 Positive guard for capability stages 1a and 1b: app-quire functions
 that perform device I/O and honestly declare the Device.* effect
 type-check. These are the sanctioned counterparts to
 errors/cap-launder-pure-io, errors/cap-launder-pure-block, and
 errors/cap-launder-pure-mmio - each effect is real and declarable,
 not a blanket ban. read-port declares Device.Port, read-sector0
 declares Device.Block, mmio-byte declares Device.Mmio, so the
 row-subset check passes on all three; the naked calls without the
 declarations are the error cases. opening stays pure and calls none
 of them, so the run is deterministic.

Section: Definitions

  read-port : Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  read-port (p) = port-in-byte p

  read-sector0 : Integer -> [Device.Block] Integer
  read-sector0 (s) = block-read-sector s

  mmio-byte : Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  mmio-byte (a) = read-mmio a 0

  opening : Text = "device-port-declares-ok"

